hadiths[165]{hadithnumber,text}:
"11221","On the authority of Qutayba, on the authority of Layth, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: “Umar decided: Concerning a slave who is sold and has money, his money belongs to his master who sold him.” “Unless the buyer makes a stipulation of his own money.”"
"11222","On the authority of Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Nafi’, that Umar: made a ruling on the property of the slave for his master, except that Buyer stipulates \ (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"11223","On the authority of Hilal bin Al-Ala, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Hushaym, on the authority of Sufyan bin Hussein, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salem bin Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of His father, on the authority of his grandfather, Omar bin Al-Khattab, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever sells a slave and has money, gets his money, unless The buyer stipulates, and whoever sells a palm tree that has been ripened, its fruit is for the seller, unless the buyer stipulates.” On the authority of Hilal bin Al-Ala, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Muhammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, with it. This is wrong, but the correct thing is the hadith of Laith bin Saad, Ubaid Allah, and Ayoub. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11224","On the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Saeed, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Omar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar, on the authority of Omar, he said: “Who He sold a slave and had money, and his money is the seller’s, unless the buyer stipulates it.” On the authority of Qutayba, on the authority of Hammad bin Zaid, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, with it. suspended"
"11225","On the authority of Al-Harith bin Miskin, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Kharijah bin Zaid bin Thabit, on the authority of his father Zaid Ibn Thabit said that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “granted the sale of naked dates and dates.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11226","On the authority of Issa bin Hammad, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of Zayd bin Thabit, that the Prophet prayed God, upon him be peace, “permitted the sale of nudes” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11227","On the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Bashir bin Yassar, on the authority of Sahl bin Abi Hathamah, The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “forbade the sale of fruit until its goodness was evident, and he permitted the sale of the fruit for its value, so that its people could eat it.” “wet” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11228","On the authority of Ishaq bin Mansour Al-Kawsaj, and Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawrqi, both of them on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Dawud bin Al-Husayn, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, the client of Abu Ahmad, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, permitted the It is sold for its price in five awsuqs, or less than five.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11229","On the authority of Yahya bin Habib, on the authority of Hammad bin Zaid, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Hanzalah bin Qais al-Zarqi al-Ansari, on the authority of Rafi’ bin Khadij, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade us from renting our land.” And at that time there was neither gold nor silver, so the man was renting. His land includes what is known about the spring and the coming days, and other known things. . . He drove him"
"11230","On the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala, on the authority of Al-Mu’tamir, on the authority of Abdul-Karim bin Malik Al-Jazari, Saeed bin Jubayr said, Ibn Abbas said: “ The best thing you can do is to rent out his land to one of you for gold and silver.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11231","On the authority of Qutayba bin Saeed, on the authority of Sufyan bin Uyaynah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Najih, on the authority of Abdullah bin Kathir, on the authority of Abu Al-Minhaal Abd al-Rahman bin Mut’im said: I heard Ibn Abbas saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to Medina, and they They used to pay dates in advance for two or three years, so he forbade them and said: “Whoever pays in advance, let him pay in advance in a specified measure and a specified weight, for a specified period.” \known\"""""""
"11232","On the authority of Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, on the authority of Issa ibn Yunus, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Abi Orouba, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted him and said: “The neighbor of the house has more right to the house.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11233","On the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Abdul-Malik bin Abi Suleiman Al-Arzami, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “The neighbor has more right to his neighbour’s intercession, and he is expected to do so, even if he is absent, if their path is the same.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11234","On the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Aziz bin Abi Rizmah, on the authority of Al-Fadl bin Musa, on the authority of Hussein bin Waqid, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, he said: “ The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, decided by pre-emption and generosity.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11235","On the authority of Yusuf bin Saeed, on the authority of Hajjaj bin Muhammad, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, decided He recognized pre-emption in every share that has not been divided, whether a quarter or a wall. It is not permissible for him to sell it until his partner gives permission. If he wishes, he can take it, and if If he wants, he can leave it, but if he sells and does not give permission, then he has more right to it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11236","On the authority of Ismail bin Masoud, on the authority of Bishr bin Al-Mufaddal, on the authority of Shu’bah. On the authority of Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, on the authority of Issa ibn Yunus, on the authority of Saeed, both of them, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Samurah ibn Jundub, on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “The neighbor of his house has more right to the neighbor’s house.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11237","On the authority of Ishaq bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Issa bin Yunus, on the authority of Hussein Al-Muallem, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Sharid, on the authority of his father Al-Sharid bin Suwayd, that a man said: O Messenger of God, on my land no one has any association or oaths except the neighbors. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “The neighbor has more right to punish him.” On the authority of Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Ammar, on the authority of Al-Mu’afa bin Imran, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdul Rahman bin Ya’la, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Sharid bin Suwayd, with it. On the authority of Muhammad bin Bashar, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Mahdi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdul Rahman bin Ya’la, on the authority of Amr bin Al Sharid, With it, and on the authority of Muhammad bin Ali bin Maimun, on the authority of Al-Faryabi, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ya’la bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Sharid, with it . On the authority of Muhammad bin Hatim, on the authority of Suwayd bin Nasr, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Maysara, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Sharid, With it, and on the authority of Ishaq bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Muslim, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Sharid, with it (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11238","On the authority of Zakaria bin Yahya, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ubaid bin Hassab, on the authority of Ismail bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib On the authority of Amr bin Al-Sharid, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The neighbor has more right to his bloodshed.” On the authority of Zakaria bin Yahya, on the authority of Abu Muammar Ismail bin Ibrahim Al-Hudhali, on the authority of Hushaym, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of a man from the Al-Sharid family, said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: . . . So he reminded him (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11239","On the authority of Ishaq bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Fadl bin Musa, on the authority of Abu Hamzah Al-Sukkari Muhammad bin Maimun, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ubaid Allah bin Abi Mulaika, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “The partner is an intercessor and the pre-emption in all “Something.” On the authority of Muhammad bin Ali bin Maymun Al-Raqi, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yusuf Al-Faryabi, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Ibn Abu Mulaika, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, similar to him, mursal (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11240","On the authority of Zakaria bin Yahya, on the authority of Harun bin Humaid, on the authority of Al-Fadl bin Anbasa, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam bin Utaiba, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, Abdullah bin Amr, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The neighbor has more right to watering His house, or his land.” . Hadith"
"11241","On the authority of Suwayd bin Nasr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of the one who told him, on the authority of Ali, And Ibn Masoud, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “decreed goodness.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11242","On the authority of Ali bin Hajar, on the authority of Sufyan bin Uyaynah, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Maysara, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Sharid, on the authority of Abu Rafi’, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “The neighbor has more right to his compensation.” On the authority of Mahmoud bin Ghailan, on the authority of Abu Nu’aym, on the authority of Sufyan al-Thawri, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Maysara, with it"
"11243","On the authority of Suleiman bin Dawud, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Abd al-Aziz al-Majishun, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa`id, and Abu Salamah Both of them, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “ruled by pre-emption in what was not divided, so if the punishments have occurred, then there is no pre-emption. On the authority of Al-Harith bin Miskin, on the authority of Ibn Al-Qasim, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Sa’id and Abu Salamah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him And he greeted him as a messenger (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11244","On the authority of Muhammad bin Hatim, on the authority of Suwayd bin Nasr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Malik and Muammar, both of them, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, that The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “decided by pre-emption what was not sworn.” On the authority of Qutaibah, on the authority of Bakr ibn Mudar, on the authority of Ja`far ibn Rabi’ah, on the authority of Bukayr ibn al-Ashjaj, on the authority of Ibn al-Musayyab, his saying (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11245","On the authority of Mujahid bin Musa, on the authority of Ismail bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Do not sell someone from a land to another, nor quarrel with each other, nor do a man bargain on the basis of his brother’s agreement, nor propose a proposal based on a proposal.” His brother, and a woman should not ask for a divorce from her sister, so that she may have enough of what is in her vessel, and let her get married, for she only gets what God has decreed for her.”"
"11246","On the authority of Qutayba bin Saeed, on the authority of Al-Layth bin Saad, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman bin Ghanj, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Prophet prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. “He gave to the Jews of Khaybar the palm trees of Khaybar and its land on the condition that they would manage it from their wealth, and that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace And he handed over half of its fruit.” On the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abd Allah bin Abd al-Hakam, on the authority of Shuaib bin al-Layth, on the authority of his father al-Layth bin Saad, with it (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11247","On the authority of Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Bukayr, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim, on the authority of his father, On the authority of Aisha, she said: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about Barira, and I wanted to buy it and stipulate loyalty to its people. He said: Buy her, for loyalty belongs to the one who frees him. He said: She was given a choice, and her husband was a slave. Then he said after that: I don’t know, I don’t know. And meat was brought to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they said: This is what was given in charity to Bareerah. He said: “It is a charity for her, and a gift for us.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11248","On the authority of Muhammad bin Mansour, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Amra, on the authority of Aisha, that Bareerah came to Aisha She asked her about her writing, and her family said: If you wish, you can give the rest of her writing, and we will have loyalty. When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came I mentioned that to him, and he said: “Buy her and emancipate her, for loyalty belongs to the one who emancipates.” Then he ascended the pulpit and said: “What’s the matter?” People stipulate conditions that are not in the Book of God. Whoever stipulates a condition that is not in the Book of God, it is not permissible for him, even if he stipulates a hundred conditions.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11249","On the authority of Ishaq bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Amra, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: “Every condition that is not in the Book of God is invalid.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11250","On the authority of Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala, on the authority of Sufyan bin Uyaynah, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salem bin Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “Whoever keeps a dog, other than a hunting or livestock dog, two qirats will be deducted from his reward every day.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11251","On the authority of Qutayba bin Saeed, on the authority of Al-Layth, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he heard him say that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever catches a dog, except a wild dog or a livestock dog, two Qirats will be deducted from his reward every day.”"
"11252","On the authority of Ishaq bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Abd al-Razzaq, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “Whoever keeps a dog, other than a hunting, agricultural or livestock dog, one Qirat will be deducted from his work every day.”"
"11253","On the authority of Yunus bin Abdul Ala, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, on the authority of Malik, and Yunus bin Yazid. On the authority of Al-Harith bin Miskin, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, on the authority of Yunus, and others, both of them - Malik and Yunus -, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Abdullah bin Utbah, on the authority of Zayd bin Khalid and Abu Hurairah, that two men came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. They would dispute over him, and one of them said: Judge between us according to the Book of God, and the other, who was the more understanding of them, said: Yes, so judge between us according to the Book of God. And he gave me permission to speak. He said: “Speak.” He said: My son was stubborn about this, and he committed adultery with his wife, so I ransomed him with a hundred A sheep and a female slave. Then I asked the people of knowledge, and they told me that my son must be subjected to a hundred lashes, and exile for a year, and stoning is for His wife. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, I will decide between you according to the Book of God. As for your sheep and your female servant, separate To you. “And he flogged his son a hundred lashes and exiled him for a year, and he commanded Anis to stone another’s wife if she confessed. So she confessed, so he stoned her.”"
"11254","On the authority of Muhammad ibn Uthman, on the authority of Bahz, on the authority of Hammad ibn Salamah, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jumhan, on the authority of Safinah, he said: Umm Salamah freed me, She made it a condition that I must serve the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, as long as he lived. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11255","On the authority of Amr bin Ali, on the authority of Ibn Mahdi, on the authority of Ikrimah bin Ammar, on the authority of Abu Zumail Samak bin Al-Walid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day of Hudaybiyyah, reconciled with the polytheists, and he said to Ali: “Write, O Ali: This is what Muhammad, the Messenger of God, reconciled with.” “God.” They said: “If we had known that you were the Messenger of God, we would not have fought you.” Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Forgive me, O Ali. Oh God, you know.” I am the Messenger of God. Erase, O Ali, and write: This is what Muhammad bin Abdullah agreed upon.” Brief, and it is a summary of the hadith of Al-Haruriyyah. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11256","On the authority of Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Ibn Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Al-Miswar ibn Makhramah and Marwan ibn Al-Hakam reported on the authority of the Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: When Suhail ibn Amr at that time, while Suhail bin Amr stipulated to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that none of us should come to you, even if he was of your religion. Unless you return him to us, and leave us alone with him, the believers disliked that and were displeased with him, and Suhail refused otherwise. On that day, he returned Abu Jandal to his father, Suhail bin Amr, and none of the men came to him without returning him during that period, even if he was a Muslim. The believing women came as migrants, and Umm Kulthum bint Uqba bin Abi Mu’it was among those who went out to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. On that day, she was freed, and her family came to ask the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, to return her to them, but he did not return her to them, because God revealed concerning them: When believing women come to you as immigrants, test them. God knows best about their faith, to His saying: Nor are they lawful for them. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11257","On the authority of Imran bin Bakkar, on the authority of Ali bin Ayyash, on the authority of Shuaib bin Abi Hamza, on the authority of Abu Al-Zinad, on the authority of Al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said The Ansar said to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: Divide the palm trees between us and our brothers. He said: No, so they said: You provide us with sufficient supplies, and we will share with you in The fruit, they said: We heard and obeyed. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11258","On the authority of Qutayba, on the authority of Abu al-Ahwas, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Ubaidah bin Amr al-Salmani, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “The best of my nation is the generation that follows me, then those that follow them, then those that follow them, then there will come peoples that will precede them.” The testimony of one of them is his oath, and his oath is his testimony.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11259","On the authority of Suwayd bin Nasr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Ibn Uyaynah, on the authority of Ziyad bin Ulaqa, on the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Shu’bah, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed until his feet swelled, and it was said to him: Have you not been forgiven for your previous sins and your future sins? He said: “Shall I not be a grateful servant?” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11260","On the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Saeed, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Sulaiman al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Usama bin Zayd, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “I stood at the gate of Paradise, and behold, most of those who enter it are the poor, but the people of greatness are imprisoned, except those of Hell. He commanded them to go to Hell, and I stood at the gate of Hell, and behold, the majority of those who entered it were women. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11261","On the authority of Bishr bin Hilal, on the authority of Imran bin Musa, on the authority of Abd al-Warith, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Raja’, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “I looked into Paradise and saw that most of its people were poor, and I looked into Hell and saw that most of its people were women.” \"" 11262"""""
"11262","On the authority of Suwayd bin Nasr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Whoever loves Meeting God, God loves meeting Him, and whoever hates meeting God, God hates meeting Him. We said: O Messenger of God, we all hate death. He said: This is not hatred of death, but when it comes to the believer, good news comes to him from God Almighty of what is about to happen to him, for there is nothing more beloved to him. From the fact that he has met God Almighty, and God loves meeting him, and if the immoral or infidel is present, he will bring him what is going to happen to him. Evil, or whatever evil is encountered, he hates meeting God, and God hates meeting it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11263","On the authority of Hanad bin Al-Sari, on the authority of Abu Zubaid, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Amer, on the authority of Shurayh bin Hani, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever loves meeting God, God will love meeting Him, and whoever hates meeting God, God will hate meeting Him.” Shurayh said: So I came. Aisha, so I said: O Mother of the Believers, I heard Abu Hurairah mentioning on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Whoever loves the meeting with God, loves God is the one who hates the meeting with him, and whoever hates God, God hates the meeting with him.” And there is not one of us who does not hate death. She said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said it. Peace and blessings of God be upon him, but not with the one you go to, but when the sight longs, and the chest grates, and the skin shivers, then in that case: whoever loves Meeting God, God loves meeting Him, and whoever hates meeting God, God hates meeting him."
"11264","On the authority of Qutayba bin Saeed, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr, on the authority of Anas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “ Three people follow the dead person: his family, his money, and his work. Two of them return: his family and his money, and one remains, which is his work. On the authority of Suwayd bin Nasr, on the authority of Ibn Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Sufyan bin Uyaynah, with"
"11265","On the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Saeed, on the authority of Muslim bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Hammam bin Yahya Al-Awdhi, on the authority of Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Abi Talha, on the authority of Anas, said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, wrote some lines and said: “This is hope, and this is its term, so while it was like that, The closest line came to him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11266","On the authority of Suwayd bin Nasr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abi Bakr bin Anas, on the authority of his grandfather Anas said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “This is the son of Adam, and this is his term.” He placed his hand at the back of his neck, then extended it. He said: “And then his hope, and then his hope.”"
"11267","On the authority of Amr bin Ali, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Sufyan Al-Thawri, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Ya’la Mundhir Al-Thawri, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ bin Khathim, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, wrote a square, and made a line in the middle, coming out of it, and made small lines to the end. This is the one in the middle, from his side which is in the middle, and he said: “This is the human being, and this is his term surrounding him, or it has surrounded him, and this The one who is outside: his hope, and these small plans: the symptoms. If this one misses him, this one will bite him, and if this one misses him, “This mauled him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11268","On the authority of Muhammad bin Adam bin Sulaiman, and Suwayd bin Nasr, both on the authority of Ibn Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “The son of Adam will grow old, and two parts of him will remain: eagerness and hope.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11269","On the authority of Harun bin Saeed, on the authority of Khalid bin Nizar, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Mabrur, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, and Ubayy Salamah, both on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “The heart of a sheikh remains young in two matters: in the love of money, and in longevity.” \Hope\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"11270","On the authority of Mahmoud bin Ghailan, on the authority of Al-Nadr bin Shumail, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Musa bin Anas, on the authority of his father Anas bin Malik, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “If you knew what I know, you would laugh a little and cry a lot.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11271","On the authority of Qutayba bin Saeed, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said “O nation of Muhammad, by God, if you knew what I know, you would laugh little and cry much.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11272","On the authority of Ali bin Muhammad bin Zakaria, on the authority of Al-Mu’affa bin Sulaiman, on the authority of Musa bin Ayan, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr bin Alqamah Bin Waqqas, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, Alqamah Bin Waqqas, on the authority of Bilal Bin Al-Harith, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “The man To speak a word out of God’s displeasure, not thinking that it will reach what it does, so God records His displeasure with it until the Day of Resurrection. A man utters a word that pleases God, not thinking that it will reach what it does, so God records His satisfaction with it until the Day of Resurrection. “The Resurrection.” On the authority of Suwayd bin Nasr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Alqamah bin Waqqas, with it. Abu Abdul Rahman said: Musa bin Uqba did not hear from Alqamah bin Waqqas. On the authority of Qutayba bin Saeed, on the authority of Malik. On the authority of Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman, on the authority of Shuaib bin Al-Layth, on the authority of Al-Layth, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, both of them are Malik, and Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr bin Alqamah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Bilal bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Ahmad bin Hafs bin Abdullah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Tahman, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr bin Alqamah bin Waqqas, on the authority of his grandfather Alqamah bin Waqqas, on the authority of Bilal bin Al-Harith Al-Muzani, the companion of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was detained. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11273","On the authority of Qutayba, on the authority of Bakr ibn Mudar, on the authority of Yazid ibn al-Hadi, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, on the authority of Issa ibn Talha, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Whenever a servant speaks a word, he will go down with it in Hellfire farther than the distance between the East and the West.” On the authority of Suwayd bin Nasr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, with it suspended (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11274","On the authority of Suwayd bin Nasr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Issa, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Al-Jaad, On the authority of Thawban, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “A man is deprived of livelihood because of the sin that befalls him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11275","On the authority of Suwayd bin Nasr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Ma’iz, on the authority of Sufyan Ibn Abdullah Al-Thaqafi said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Say: I believe in God, then be upright.” On the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna, on the authority of Ibn Dawud, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Saad, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman bin Ma’iz , on the authority of Sufyan bin Abdullah Al-Thaqafi, and the like. On the authority of Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim, on the authority of. . . , on the authority of Ibrahim bin Saad, with it (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11276","On the authority of Qutayba bin Saeed, on the authority of Al-Layth bin Saad, on the authority of Saeed Al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Shurayh Al-Khuza’i, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: “Whoever believes in God and the Last Day, let him say good or remain silent,” and on the authority of Ali bin Shuaib, on the authority of Maan bin Isa, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Sa`id al-Maqbari, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Miskin, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of al-Maqbari, on the authority of (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11277","On the authority of Suwayd bin Nasr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “Whoever believes in God and the Last Day, let him speak good or remain silent.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11278","On the authority of Suwayd bin Nasr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Saeed Al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “Whoever believes in God and the Last Day, let him speak good, or let him remain silent.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11279","On the authority of Ali bin Hajar, on the authority of Jarir, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, on the authority of Ward, the writer of Al-Mughirah bin Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Shu`bah, that he wrote to Muawiyah: I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “God hates three things for you: gossip, and wasting money.” “And asking a lot of questions, and forbidding disobedience to mothers, and killing daughters, and forbidding them to commit fraud.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11280","On the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Muhammad bin Salam, on the authority of Hajjaj bin Muhammad, on the authority of Al-Layth bin Saad, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Saleh, on the authority of Abdul Rahman Ibn Jubayr Ibn Nufayr, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: O Abu Dharr, do you see the abundance of money? Is it wealth? I said: Yes, O Messenger of God. He said: Do you think that lack of money is poverty? I said: Yes, O Messenger of God. He said: “Wealth is the richness of the heart, and poverty is the poverty of the heart.” Then he asked me about a man from the Quraysh, and he said: Do you know so-and-so? I said: Yes, O Messenger of God. He said: How do you see him or her? I said: If he asks, he is given, and if he comes, he is brought in. Then he asked me about a man from the people of Suffah, and he said: “Do you know so-and-so?” I said: No, by God, I do not know him, O Messenger of God. He said: And he continued sweetening it and calling it, until I recognized him, so I said: I recognized him, O The Messenger of God, he said: “So how do you see him or her? "" 11281"""",""On the authority of Harun bin Abdullah, on the authority of Maan bin Issa, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Wealth is not the abundance of wealth, but rather the wealth of the soul.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"11281","On the authority of Harun ibn Abdullah, from Ma'n ibn Isa, from Malik, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Indeed Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says on the Day of Resurrection: 'O son of Adam, I commanded you to pray the Fajr prayer, but you did not pray it.'"""""
"11282","On the authority of Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, on the authority of Muadh ibn Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Yunus ibn Abi al-Furat al-Iskaf, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, he said: “ The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, did not eat in a tent or in a trough, nor did he have his bread unleavened. He said: And I said to Qatada: What kind of food were they? Do they eat? He said: On travel"
"11283","On the authority of Qutayba bin Saeed, on the authority of Yaqoub bin Abdul Rahman Al-Qari, on the authority of Abu Hazim, he said: I asked Sahl bin Saad: Did the Messenger of God eat? The pure one, may God bless him and grant him peace? Sahl said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not see al-Naqi from the time God sent him until God took him.” He said: So I said: Was it? Did you have sieves during the era of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not see a sieve from the time God sent him until God took him.” He said: I said: How did you eat? Barley, not sifted? He said: We used to grind it and blow it, and whatever it flew would fly, and whatever was left we ground it and ate it."
"11284","On the authority of Qutayba, on the authority of Yahya bin Zakaria bin Abi Zaida, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Qais bin Abi Hazim, on the authority of Saad Ibn Abi Waqqas said: “We used to fight with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we had no food to eat except brown leaves.”"
"11285","On the authority of Suwayd bin Nasr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Suleiman bin Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Humaid bin Hilal, on the authority of Khalid bin Umair Al-Adawi said: Utba bin Ghazwan addressed us, and he thanked God and praised him, then he said: As for what follows, the world has given us permission. Basram, and she put on a shoe, for there is nothing left of it except a sap, like the sap of a vessel whose owner pours it, and you move from it. To an abode that will never disappear, so move with what is best for you, for it has been mentioned to us that a stone is thrown from the brink of Hell and falls into it. Seventy years without a bottom. By God, they will be filled. Are you astonished? It has been mentioned to us that the distance between the two gates of Paradise is a journey of forty years, and a day will come upon it when it will be extremely crowded. You saw me while I was seven with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we had no food except the leaves of the trees. A Burdah, so I split it between me and Saad bin Malik, and I girded myself with half of it, and he shirked itself with half of it, and none of us are alive today. Unless he becomes a prince over one of the countries of Egypt, I seek refuge in God from being great in myself and small in the sight of God, and it was not “There is no prophecy unless it is abrogated, until its outcome becomes kingship, and you will be tried, or you will try the princes after me.”"
"11286","From Qutaybah, from Ya'qub ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Qari, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: ""We used to rejoice on the day of Friday..."""""
"11287","On the authority of Amr bin Mansour, on the authority of Adam, on the authority of Al-Layth bin Saad, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Salih, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Jubayr bin Nufayr, On the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, he said: While I was in the mosque, a group of poor immigrants were sitting, when he sat The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to them, so I stood up to them and said: “Let the poor immigrants be given good tidings of what will please their faces, for they will enter Paradise forty years before the rich.” I saw their colors so bright that I wished I were one of them."
"11288","On the authority of Suwayd bin Nasr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Haywa bin Shurayh, on the authority of Abu Hani Al-Khawlani, on the authority of Abu Ali Al-Janabi, on the authority of Fadalah bin Ubaid, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Blessed is he who is guided to Islam, and whose livelihood is sufficient and content.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11289","On the authority of Suwayd bin Nasr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Haywa bin Shurayh, on the authority of Abu Hani’ Al-Khawlani, on the authority of Abu Ali Al-Janabi On the authority of Fadalah bin Ubaid, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “The mujahid is he who strives himself for the sake of God Almighty.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11290","On the authority of Amr bin Mansour, on the authority of Adam, on the authority of Al-Layth bin Saad, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Salih, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Jubayr bin Nufayr, On the authority of his father, on the authority of Ka’b ibn Iyadh al-Ash’ari, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Indeed, every nation has a temptation, and the temptation of my nation is money.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11291","On the authority of Suwayd bin Nasr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Zakaria bin Abi Zaida, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman bin Saad bin Zurara, on the authority of Ibn Ka’b ibn Malik al-Ansari, on the authority of his father, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “They are not hungry wolves.” They were sent with sheep that are more corrupt than a man’s eagerness for money and honor for his religion.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11292","On the authority of Suwayd bin Nasr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Qais bin Abi Hazim, on the authority of the importer Ibn Shaddad Al-Fihri, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The world in the Hereafter is nothing but like one of you putting his finger into the sea. Let him see what you will return with.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11293","On the authority of Suwayd bin Nasr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Omar, on the authority of Khubayb bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Hafs bin Asim bin Omar bin Al-Khattab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There are seven whom God will shade on the Day of Resurrection in His shade on the Day when there will be no shade but his shade: a just imam, a young man who grew up in the worship of God, a man who mentioned God in private and his eyes overflowed, and a man whose heart Hanging in the mosque, and two men who loved each other for the sake of God, and a man who was invited by a woman of position and beauty to herself and he said: I fear God, and a man He gave charity and hid it so that his left hand would not know what his right hand had done.”"
"11294","On the authority of Suwayd bin Nasr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Thabit Al-Bunani, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of his father, he said: I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was praying, and his stomach was buzzing like the buzzing of a cauldron, meaning: he was crying. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11295","On the authority of Suwayd bin Nasr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Abdullah bin Saeed bin Abi Hind, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “There are two blessings of which many people are neglected: health and free time.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11296","On the authority of Qutayba bin Saeed, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of Al-Ja’d Abu Uthman, on the authority of Abu Raja’ Al-Ataridi, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace, in what is narrated on the authority of his Lord, Blessed and Most High: “Indeed, your Lord is Merciful. Whoever intends to do a good deed and does not do it, it is recorded for him as a good deed.” If he does it, it will be recorded for him as ten, up to seven hundred, or many times over. And whoever intends to do an evil deed and does not do it, a good deed is recorded for him. If he does it, it will be recorded as one, or God will erase it, and none will perish before God except one who perishes.”"
"11297","On the authority of Suwayd bin Nasr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Mubarak, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yassar, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Safwan bin Mahrez, on the authority of Ibn Omar, he said: While I was walking with him, a man came to him and said: O Ibn Omar, how did you hear the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, mentioned in the disputes? He said: I heard him say: “The believer approaches his Lord, the Mighty and Majestic, until He places His protection over him.” So he mentioned his sheet of paper, and said: “So He rebukes him for his sins.” Do you know? He says: My Lord I know. He says: Do you know? He says: Yes, my Lord I know, until he achieves what God wills. He reaches it, then he says: “I have concealed it from you, and I forgive you today.” He said: “So he will be given a record of his good deeds, and as for the disbeliever, he will be called.” On the heads of the witnesses, God Almighty said: And these witnesses say, who lied about their Lord: “Surely, the curse of God is upon the wrongdoers.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11298","On the authority of Muhammad bin Ali bin Maimun, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yusuf, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Abdah bin Abi Lubabah, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: He took The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with some of my body, and he said: “Worship God as if you see Him, and be in this world as if you are a stranger or a passerby.” \way\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"11299","On the authority of Suwayd bin Nasr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed Al-Ansari, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Taymi, on the authority of Alqamah bin Waqqas, on the authority of Omar bin Al-Khattab, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Actions are based on intention, and a person only gets what he intends.” So whoever’s emigration is to God and His Messenger, then his emigration is to God and His Messenger, and whoever’s emigration is to this world He marries her or a woman he marries, so his migration is to what he migrated to.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11300","On the authority of Suwayd bin Nasr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Haywa bin Shurayh, on the authority of Bakr bin Amr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Hubayra On the authority of Abu Tamim Al-Jishani, on the authority of Omar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “If only you put your trust in God as He deserves, “You will be provided with just as birds are provided. They go in the morning exhausted and go away feeling exhausted.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11301","On the authority of Suwayd bin Nasr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Musab bin Saad bin Abi Waqqas, that Hafsa said to Omar: Don’t you wear a softer garment than yours and eat better food than yours? He said: I will dispute with you over your soul, and he began to remind her of what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had been in, and what effort he had been in until... He made her cry, and said: I told you: “I had two companions who took a path other than theirs, and I took a path other than theirs. He took a path other than theirs, and I By God, I will share with them a life similar to theirs, perhaps I will be able to live with them in their comfortable life.”"
"11302","On the authority of Suwayd bin Nasr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Imran Al-Juni, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Samit, on the authority of Abu Dharr, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “If you cook a pot, add a lot of broth, then see the household of your neighbors. So treat them with kindness.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11303","On the authority of Ahmad ibn Yahya, on the authority of Abu Nu`aym, on the authority of Omar ibn Dhar, on the authority of Mujahid, that Abu Hurairah used to say: God, there is no god but It is, if I were to support my liver on the ground due to hunger, and if I were to drag a stone on my stomach due to hunger, and I sat on their way one day From which they come out, so Abu Bakr passed by, and I asked him about a verse from the Book of God. I only asked him to satisfy me, so he passed by and did not do so, then Omar passed by me, and I asked him about a verse from the Book of God. I only asked him to satisfy me, but he passed by and did not do so. Then Abu al-Qasim, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by me. Peace be upon him. He smiled when he saw me and recognized what was on my face. Then he said: “Abu Hurr.” I said: At your service, O Messenger of God. He said: “The truth,” and he went on. So I followed him, and he entered. He asked for permission, so he gave me permission. Then he entered and found milk in a cup. He said: “Where did this milk come from?” They said: Give it to him as a gift. For you is so-and-so or so-and-so. He said: “Abu Hurr.” I said: At your command, O Messenger of God. He said: “Go to the people of Suffah and call them for me.” He said: The people of Suffah are the guests of Islam. They do not seek refuge with family, money, or anyone. If he receives charity, he sends it to them, and does not take it as a gift. Some of it, and when a gift came to him, he sent it to them, and he took some of it and shared it with them. That upset me, and I said: What is this milk in? People of Suffa? ! I had the right to have a drink of this milk to strengthen myself, so when my command came, I would give it to them, as long as it was possible that they would inform me. Who is this milk? ! There was no need to obey God and His Messenger, may God bless him and grant him peace, so I went to them, and I called them, and they came, and they asked for permission, and he gave permission. To them, and they took their seats from the house. He said: “O Abu Hurr.” I said: At your command, O Messenger of God. He said: “Take it and give it to them.” He said: So I took the cup and gave it to the man, so he drank until he had enough of it, then he returned the cup to me, so I gave it to the man and he drank until he had enough, then He would return the cup to me, and he would drink until he had quenched his thirst, then he would return the cup to me, until I reached the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the people had narrated it. All of them, so he took the cup and placed it on his hand. He looked at me and smiled, and said: “Abu Hurr.” I said: At your service, O Messenger of God. He said: You and I remain.” I said: You have spoken the truth, O Messenger of God. He said: “Sit down and drink.” So I sat down and drank. He said: “Drink,” so I drank, but I did not He kept saying, “Drink,” until I said, “No.” By the One who has sent you with the truth, I cannot find a way for him. He said, “Show me,” so I gave him the cup, and he thanked God. He said the name and drank the waste (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11304","On the authority of Ishaq bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Usama, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Amara bin Al-Qaqa’ bin Shubramah, on the authority of Abu Zar’ah, on the authority of Abu Huraira, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O God, make the livelihood of the family of Muhammad sufficient.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11305","On the authority of Suwayd bin Nasr, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of Suleiman bin Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Humaid bin Hilal, he said: Abu Qatada and Abu The demagogues. They used to travel to Mecca frequently. They said: We came across a man from the desert. The Bedouin said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took my hand. Peace be upon him, and he began to teach me what God had taught him, and one of the things I memorized from him was that he said: “Do not neglect anything out of fear of God, unless God gives you something better than it.” \"" 11306"""""
"11306","On the authority of Ishaq bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Amer Al-Aqdi, on the authority of Saeed bin Muslim bin Banak, on the authority of Amer bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Awf bin Al-Harith bin Al-Tufayl, Aisha’s infant, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Beware of despicable deeds. For she has a seeker from God.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11307","On the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ismail bin Suleiman, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Raja’ Al-Makki, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Aisha, On the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “Aim and approach, and know that none of you will take his deeds into Paradise, even if the deeds are most beloved to God.” “I always do it, even if it is small.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11308","On the authority of Imran bin Musa, on the authority of Abdul-Warith, on the authority of Abdul-Aziz bin Suhaib, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “ Oh God, there is no good except the best of the Hereafter, so bless the Ansar and the Muhajirs.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11309","On the authority of Ishaq bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Nadr bin Shumail, on the authority of Shu’bah bin Al-Hajjaj, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said May God bless him and grant him peace: “O God, what is good is the best of the Hereafter, forgive the Ansar and the Emigrants.”"
"11310","On the authority of Ishaq bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Nadr bin Shumail, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Qurrah, on the authority of Anas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “O God, what is good is the best of the Hereafter, so make good the Ansar and the Emigrants.”"
"11311","On the authority of Qutayba bin Saeed, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Abi Hazim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Sahl bin Saad, he said: We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. peace be upon him in the ditch, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O God, there is no life except the life of the Hereafter, so forgive the Muhajireen and the Ansar.”"
"11312","On the authority of Suwayd bin Nasr, on the authority of Ibn Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Muammar, and Yunus, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Al-Miswar bin Makramah On the authority of Amr bin Awf Al-Ansari, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent Abu Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah, and he came with money from Bahrain. The Ansar heard of the arrival of Abu Ubaidah, so they performed the dawn prayer with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed He left, and they confronted him. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, smiled when he saw them, then said: “I think you have heard that Abu Did Ubaida come with anything? They said: Yes, O Messenger of God. He said: “So give good news. Hope for what pleases you. By God, what is poverty? I fear for you. But I fear that the world will be extended to you, just as it was extended to those before you, so you will compete for it as you competed with it, and it will destroy you as you did. \I destroyed them\"""""""
"11313","On the authority of Al-Rabi’ bin Sulaiman bin Dawud, on the authority of Ishaq bin Bakr, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab and Urwa bin Al-Zubayr, both of them, on the authority of Hakim bin Hazzam, who said: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he gave me, then I asked him and he gave me. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: O Wise One, “This money is green and sweet, so whoever takes it generously will A soul will be blessed for it, and whoever takes it with the supervision of a soul, he will not be blessed for it, and he is like one who eats and is not satisfied, and the upper hand is better. From the lower hand.” A wise man said: I said: O Messenger of God, by the One who sent you with the truth, I will not be with anyone after you until I part with this world for a bit."
"11314","On the authority of Qutayba bin Sa’id, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yazid, on the authority of Abu Sa’id al-Khudri, that some of the Ansar They asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he gave them. Then they asked him and he gave them, until he ran out of what he had. He said: “Whatever I have of Good, I will not withhold it from you, and whoever is chaste, God will pardon him, and whoever is patient, God will grant him patience. And no one has been given a gift that is better and more comprehensive than Patience,” on the authority of Al-Harith bin Miskin, on the authority of Ibn Al-Qasim, on the authority of Malik, with it"
"11315","On the authority of Harun bin Abdullah, on the authority of Maan, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yasar Al-Madani, on the authority of Abu Saeed, On the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “This money is green and sweet, so whoever takes it in his due right, what a wonderful aid he will be.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11316","On the authority of Qutayba bin Saeed, on the authority of Yaqoub bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Hazim Salama bin Dinar, on the authority of Saeed Al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Whoever God lives for sixty years, He has given him an excuse during his life.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11317","On the authority of Amr bin Yazid, on the authority of Saif bin Ubaid Allah and he was trustworthy, on the authority of Salamah bin Ayyar, on the authority of Saeed bin Abdul Aziz, on the authority of Al-Zuhri On the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: We said: O Messenger of God, will we see our Lord? He said: “Do you see the sun on a day with no clouds, and do you see the moon on a night with no clouds?” We said: Yes. He said: Indeed, you will see your Lord."
"11318","From Suwayd ibn Naṣr, from Ibn al-Mubārak, from Ḥaywah ibn Shurayḥ, from Abū ʿUthmān al-Walīd ibn Abī al-Walīd al-Madanī, that ʿUqbah ibn Muslim narrated to him that Shufayy narrated to him that he entered al-Madīnah and found a man around whom the people had gathered. He said: 'Who is this?' They said: 'Abū Hurayrah.' He drew near to him until he sat before him while he was narrating to the people. When he fell silent and was alone, he said to him: 'I ask you by the right and by the right, narrate to me a ḥadīth you heard from the Messenger of Allāh ﷺ, which you understood and learned.' Abū Hurayrah said: 'I shall do so. I shall narrate to you a ḥadīth which the Messenger of Allāh ﷺ narrated to me, which I understood and learned.' Then Abū Hurayrah gasped, and we remained a short while, after which he regained consciousness and said: 'I shall narrate to you a ḥadīth which the Messenger of Allāh ﷺ narrated to me in this house, with no one present besides me and him.' Then Abū Hurayrah gasped severely, then regained consciousness, wiped his face, and said: 'I shall do so. I shall narrate to you a ḥadīth which the Messenger of Allāh ﷺ narrated to me while he and I were in this house, with no one present besides me and him.' Then Abū Hurayrah gasped severely, then fell forward on his face, and I supported him for a long time. Then he regained consciousness and said: 'The Messenger of Allāh ﷺ narrated to me that Allāh, Blessed and Exalted, when it is the Day of Resurrection, will descend to His servants to judge between them, and every nation will be kneeling. The first ones He will call upon will be: a man who memorized the Qurʾān, a man who was killed in the cause of Allāh, and a man of great wealth.

Allāh will say to the reciter: ""Did I not teach you what I revealed to My Messenger?"" He will say: ""Yes, O my Lord."" He will say: ""What did you do with what you learned?"" He will say: ""I used to stand in prayer with it during the hours of the night and the hours of the day."" Allāh will say to him: ""You have lied."" The angels will say: ""You have lied."" Allāh will say: ""Rather, you wanted it to be said: 'So-and-so is a reciter.' And that has indeed been said.""

The wealthy man will be brought, and Allāh will say to him: ""Did I not give you ample provision so that I left you in need of no one?"" He will say: ""Yes, O my Lord."" He will say: ""What did you do with what I gave you?"" He will say: ""I used to maintain the ties of kinship and give charity."" Allāh will say to him: ""You have lied."" The angels will say: ""You have lied."" Allāh will say: ""Rather, you wanted it to be said: 'So-and-so is generous.' And that has indeed been said.""

The one who was killed in the cause of Allāh will be brought, and Allāh will say to him: ""For what were you killed?"" He will say: ""I was commanded to strive in Your cause, so I fought until I was killed."" Allāh, the Most High, will say to him: ""You have lied."" The angels will say: ""You have lied."" Allāh will say: ""Rather, you wanted it to be said: 'So-and-so is brave.' And that has indeed been said.""'

Then the Messenger of Allāh ﷺ struck my knees and said: 'O Abū Hurayrah, those three are the first of Allāh's creation for whom the Fire will be kindled on the Day of Resurrection.'""

Al-Walīd Abū ʿUthmān said: ʿUqbah ibn Muslim informed me that it was Shufayy who entered upon Muʿāwiyah and informed him of this. Abū ʿUthmān said: And al-ʿAlāʾ ibn Abī Ḥakīm narrated to me that he was a sword-bearer of Muʿāwiyah. A man entered upon Muʿāwiyah and informed him of this from Abū Hurayrah. Muʿāwiyah said: 'This has been done to these three. Then what about the rest of the people?' Muʿāwiyah then wept profusely until we thought he would perish, and we said: 'This man has brought us evil news.' Then Muʿāwiyah regained consciousness, wiped his face, and said: 'Allāh and His Messenger have spoken the truth: *Whoever desires the life of this world and its adornments, We will fully repay them for their deeds therein, and they will not be wronged therein. Those are the ones for whom there is nothing in the Hereafter except the Fire. And worthless is what they did therein, and vain is what they used to do* (Q 10:15–16).'"""
"11319","On the authority of Muhammad bin Salamah, and Al-Harith bin Miskin, both on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A man who has never done good said: If he dies, burn him, and leave half of him in the wilderness.” And half of it is in the sea. By God, if God decrees it, He will punish it with a punishment that no one of the worlds will punish. So God commanded the sea and it gathered what was in it. And he commanded the righteous, so he collected what was in it, then he said: Why did you do it? He said: Out of fear of you, and you know best, so he was forgiven. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11320","On the authority of Yusuf bin Saeed, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “Three people went out walking, and rain fell on them. They entered a cave in a mountain, and a rock fell on them. He said: So he said: one to another: Pray to God for the best work you have done, and one of them said: Oh God, I had two old parents, so I used to go out and tend. Then I will come and milk, then I will bring the milk, and I will bring it to my parents, and they will drink, then I will give water to the girls, my family, and my wife, and I will be held back. One night, I came and saw them both sleeping. He said: I hated to wake them up, while the boys were making out at my feet. This has always been my habit. He continued with them until dawn came, O God, if You know that I did that seeking Your Face, then release for us a window from which we can see the sky. He said: So he released them, and the other said: Oh God, if you knew that I loved a woman from my cousins as much as a man loves women, so she said You will not get that from her until you give her a hundred dinars. So I ran through it until I collected it. When I sat between her legs, she said: Fear God, and do not disperse. The ring except as it deserves, so I got up and left it. If you know that I did that seeking your face, then give us some relief. He said: so he relieved us. Of them two-thirds, and the other said: Oh God, if you know that I hired a worker for a difference of an atom and gave it to him, and that one refused to take So I went to that part and planted it, until I bought cows from him and their shepherd, then he came and said: O Abdullah, give me my right, so I said: Go to those cows and herd them, for they are yours. He said: Are you mocking me? He said: I said: I am not mocking you, but they are yours. Oh God, if you know that I did that seeking your face, then release us and reveal them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11321","On the authority of Suwayd bin Nasr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather Abdullah bin Amr, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The arrogant will be gathered on the Day of Resurrection like atoms, in the images of men. Humiliation will cover them from every place, and they will be driven to a prison in hell called Paul. The fire of the pyres will rise above them, and they will be made to drink of the juice of the people of Hell. \the clay of immorality\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"11322","On the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Saeed, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Sulaiman al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Usama bin Zayd, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “I stood at the gate of Paradise and saw that most of those entering it were the poor, except that those who are in earnest are imprisoned, except for the people of Hell. So he commanded them to go to Hell, and I stood at the gate of Hell, and behold, a crowd of those entering it were women.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11323","On the authority of Amr bin Ali, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi, on the authority of Salam bin Abi Muti’, on the authority of Abu Imran al-Juni, on the authority of Jundub, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Read the Qur’an whatever your hearts agree upon, and if you disagree upon it, then stand up.”"
"11324","On the authority of Ali bin Muhammad bin Ali, on the authority of Dawud bin Muadh, on the authority of Hammad bin Zaid, on the authority of Abu Imran Al-Juni, on the authority of Abdullah bin Rabah Al-Ansari, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, said: I migrated to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, one day, and he heard two men disagreeing. In a verse from the Book of God, he came out and anger was evident on his face, and he said: “Those who were before you perished only because of their differences in the Book.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11325","On the authority of Suwayd ibn Nasr, on the authority of Ibn al-Mubarak, on the authority of Muammar, and Yunus, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa ibn al-Zubayr, on the authority of al-Miswar ibn Makhramah, on the authority of Amr bin Awf Al-Ansari, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent Abu Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah, and he presented with money from Bahrain, and the Ansar heard of the arrival of Abu Ubaidah, so they performed the dawn prayer with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and when the Messenger of God prayed May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he left, and they confronted him. The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, smiled when he saw them, then he said: “I think you are.” Did you hear that Abu Ubaidah came with something?” They said: “Yes, O Messenger of God.” He said: “So give good news, and hope for what pleases you, for by God, what is poverty?” I fear for you, but I fear that the world will be extended to you as it was extended to those before you, so you will compete with it as they competed with it. Then it will destroy you just as it destroyed them.”"
"11326","On the authority of Suwayd bin Nasr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Ja’far bin Burqan, on the authority of Ziyad bin Al-Jarrah, on the authority of Amr bin Maymun, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to a man while he was advising him: “Take advantage of five things before five things: your youth before your old age, and your health.” Before your sickness, your wealth before your poverty, your free time before your work, and your life before your death.”"
"11327","On the authority of Suwayd bin Nasr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah, on the authority of Abu Al-Duha, on the authority of Masruq, he said: A man from the people of Mecca said to me: This is the shrine of your brother Tamim al-Dari. I saw him one night until morning, or he was anxious to read in the morning. A verse from the Book of God: He kneels and prostrates and weeps: Or are those who commit evil deeds sufficient?"
"11328","On the authority of Suwayd bin Nasr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qais bin Abi Hazim, he said: I heard Al-Zubayr bin Al-Awwam, He says: “Whoever is able to have any good deed, let him do it.”"
"11329","On the authority of Suwayd bin Nasr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Suleiman Al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Uthman Al-Nahdi, on the authority of Salman Al-Farisi, he said: “ If a man is in a dry land, he performs ablution, and if he does not find water, he performs ablution, then he calls for prayer, then he establishes it and then prays it, except for those who have prayed. The soldiers of God are arrayed.” Abdullah said: “Sufyan added to me, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Ibn Abi Uthman, on the authority of Salman: “They bow as he bows, And they prostrate with his prostration, and believe in his supplication.”"
"11330","On the authority of Suwayd bin Nasr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qais, he said: Ibn Rawaha cried, and his wife cried, He said to her: What makes you cry? She said: I cried when I saw you crying, and Abdullah said: “I know that I will enter Hell, so I do not know whether I will be saved from it or not?”"
"11331","On the authority of Suwayd bin Nasr, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of Malik bin Mughal, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Maysara, that he went to bed, He said: I wish my mother had not given birth to me. Then his wife said: O Abu Maysara, God has been good to you. He guided you to Islam. He said: Yes, “but God has made clear to us that we will enter the Fire, and He has not made clear to us that we will emerge from it.”"
"11332","On the authority of Suwayd bin Nasr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abdul-Malik bin Maysara Al-Zarraad, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, On the authority of Ibn Abbas, in the Almighty’s saying: “And their father was righteous. He said: They preserved the righteousness of their father, but no righteousness was mentioned of them.”"
"11333","On the authority of Suwayd bin Nasr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Qais bin Habatar, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: He said He has a man: a man of little work, few sins, I admire you, or a man of much work, many sins? He said: “I do not equate anything with safety.”"
"11334","On the authority of Suwayd bin Nasr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Yahya Al-Qatat, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “ The earth weeps over the believer for forty mornings.”"
"11335","On the authority of Suwayd bin Nasr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq, that He said to his tongue: “This brought me resources.”"
"11336","On the authority of Suwayd bin Nasr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Qais bin Muslim, on the authority of Tariq bin Shihab, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud said: “A man leaves his house, carrying his debt, and then returns without having anything with him...”, Hadith."
"11337","On the authority of Suwayd bin Nasr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Hilal Al-Wazzan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Aqeem, I heard that Ibn Masoud started with an oath before speaking, and said: “By God, there is not one of you who will not be alone with his Lord, then he will say: O son of Adam, what? Did you answer the messengers?"
"11338","On the authority of Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Ali bin Saeed Al-Maruzi, on the authority of Abu Kurayb, on the authority of Abu Usama, on the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, said: Abdullah was brought a drink, and he said: Give him Alqamah, he said: I am fasting, he said: He gave me black, he said: I am fasting He said: Give food to so-and-so. He said: I am fasting. They all said: I am fasting. Abdullah said: I am not fasting. So he took it and drank. Then he said: “They fear a day when hearts and eyes will be turned.”"
"11339","On the authority of Suwayd bin Nasr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: “ “It is sufficient sin for a man to narrate everything he hears.”"
"11340","On the authority of Suwayd bin Nasr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Fitr bin Khalifa, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdul God said: “The believer sees his sins as if he were under a rock, fearing that it might fall on him, and the disbeliever sees his sins as if he were under a rock, afraid that it might fall on him. A fly passed by his nose.”"
"11341","On the authority of Suwayd bin Nasr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Zubaid Al-Ayami, he said: He once said: Abdullah said about this The verse: “Fear God as He deserves to be feared.” He said: “The right to fear Him is to be obeyed and not disobeyed, to be thanked and not disbelieved, and to be remembered and not forgotten.” He said Once: Abdullah said: And he gave money out of love for it. He said: And you are eager and stingy, hoping for wealth and fearing poverty."
"11342","On the authority of Suwayd bin Nasr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of his father, he said: Omar heard a voice A man was in the mosque and said: Do you know where you are? \"" 11343"""""
"11343","From Suwayd ibn Nasr, from 'Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir, from Isma'il ibn 'Ubayd Allah ibn Abi al-Muhajir al-Makhzumi, from Umm al-Darda', who said: Abu al-Darda' fainted, then regained consciousness. He found his son Bilal with him, so he said: ""Stand up, go away from me."" Then he said: ""Who works for the like of this resting-place of mine? Who works for the like of this hour of mine? 'And We will turn away their hearts and their eyes just as they refused to believe in it the first time, and We will leave them in their transgression, wandering blindly' (Qur'an 6:110)."""""
"11344","On the authority of Suwayd bin Nasr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Aoun bin Abdullah bin Ataba bin Masoud, He said: I said to Umm al-Darda’: Which type of worship did Abu al-Darda’ have the most? She said: “Contemplation and consideration.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11345","On the authority of Suwayd bin Nasr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Al-Miswar bin It was perforated. He said: “Some people’s graves have disappeared. If they had seen me sitting with you, they would have been ashamed.”"
"11346","On the authority of Suwayd bin Nasr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Burdah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha said: “Indeed, you neglect the best form of worship: humility.”"
"11347","On the authority of Suwayd bin Nasr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Urwa, he said: Aisha wrote To Muawiyah: As for what follows, “Fear God, for if you fear God, people are sufficient for you, and if you fear people, they will not be of use to you at all before God.”"
"11348","On the authority of Suwayd bin Nasr, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of Suleiman, who is Al-Amash, on the authority of Khaythamah, who is Ibn Abdul-Rahman, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Qais Al-Jufi’i said: “If you want a good thing, do not postpone it until tomorrow, and if you have another matter, then stay as long as you can. In the affairs of this world, focus on it. If you are praying and Satan says: You are showing off, then increase it in length.”"
"11349","On the authority of Imran bin Bakkar, on the authority of Ali bin Ayyash, on the authority of Shuaib bin Abi Hamza, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Angels succeed one another among you at night and angels during the day, and they gather in the dawn prayer and in the morning prayer.” Asr, then those who were among you will come to Him, and He will ask them, and He knows best, and He will say: How did you leave My servants? They said: We left them to pray “And We brought them to pray,” on the authority of Ahmad ibn Hafs ibn Abdullah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Tahman, on the authority of Musa ibn Uqba, On the authority of Abu Al-Zinad, with it (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11350","On the authority of Ahmad bin Sulaiman, on the authority of Affan, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Abu Rafi’, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “The angels of the night and the angels of the day gather at the dawn prayer and the afternoon prayer, and when the angels of the day come back, God Almighty said to them: Where did you come from? They say: We came to you from your servants. We came to them while they were praying, and we came to you while they were praying. They prayed, and when the angels of the night came, God Almighty said to them: Where did you come from? They said: We came to you from your servants. We came to them? And they are praying, and we have come to you while they are praying.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11351","On the authority of Amr bin Uthman bin Saeed, on the authority of his father, and Baqiyya bin Al-Walid, both on the authority of Shuaib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab And Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The prayer of all of you is superior to the prayer of one of you alone by five times.” And twenty parts, and the angels of the night and the angels of the day will gather in the Fajr prayer.” Then Abu Hurairah says: So recite if you wish: The dawn recitation was witnessed (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11352","On the authority of Kathir bin Ubaid, on the authority of Muhammad bin Harb, on the authority of Al-Zubaidi, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A man’s prayer in congregation is twenty-five times greater than his prayer alone, and angels gather.” The night and the angels of the day (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11353","On the authority of Ahmad bin Saeed Al-Rabbati, on the authority of Wahb bin Jarir bin Hazim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The angels pray over one of you as long as he is in the place where he prayed. They say: O God, forgive him.” , O God, have mercy on him, O God, accept his repentance, as long as he did not harm him, what he did not inflict on him,” and on the authority of Mahmoud bin Ghaylan, on the authority of Abu Dawud, on the authority of Shu'bah, on the authority of Al-A'mash, with it. On the authority of Ahmad bin Sulaiman, and Al-Qasim bin Zakaria, both on the authority of Hussein bin Ali, on the authority of Zaida bin Qudamah, on the authority of Al-Amash, with it. On the authority of Abu Bakr bin Nafi’, on the authority of Umayyah bin Khaled, on the authority of Wahib, on the authority of Mus’ab bin Muhammad bin Shurahbil, on the authority of Abu Salih, with it (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11354","On the authority of Ahmad ibn Sulayman, on the authority of Yazid ibn Harun, on the authority of Hisham ibn Hassan, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “The angels pray over one of you as long as he is in his place of prayer, unless that happens. They say: O God, forgive him, O God, have mercy on him.” “And, on the authority of Ishaq bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Khalid bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, with it. On the authority of Amr ibn Zurarah, on the authority of Ismail ibn Ulayya, on the authority of Ayoub al-Sakhtiyani, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, with it Suspended. On the authority of Suleiman bin Salam, on the authority of Al-Nadr bin Shumail, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, with a chain of transmission. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11355","On the authority of Amr bin Ali, on the authority of Abu Asim, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Al-Ala bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Ishaq bin Abdullah Mawla Zaida, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “When he prays, meaning a Muslim, then sits in his place of prayer, you will still The angels pray for him unless it happens, saying: O God, forgive him, O God, have mercy on him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11356","On the authority of Muhammad bin Khalid bin Khalili, on the authority of Bishr bin Shuaib bin Abi Hamza. On the authority of Imran bin Bakkar, on the authority of Ali bin Ayyash, both of them are Bishr, and Ali, on the authority of Shuaib bin Abi Hamza, on the authority of Abu Al-Zinad, on the authority of Al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The angels pray over one of you as long as he is in the place where he prayed.” What did not happen: O God, forgive him, O God, have mercy on him,” and on the authority of Muhammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, with it, On the authority of Qutaibah, on the authority of Al-Mughirah ibn Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, with it. On the authority of Muhammad bin Adam bin Sulaiman, on the authority of Abdah bin Sulaiman, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, with it (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11357","On the authority of Qutayba bin Saeed, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Sumayy, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If the imam says: Not upon whom is anger nor gone astray, then say: Amen, for whoever’s words agree with the words of the angels, his sins will be forgiven.” He came forward from his sin.” On the authority of Suwayd bin Nasr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Malik, with it. On the authority of Al-Harith bin Miskin, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Al-Qasim, on the authority of Malik, with"
"11358","On the authority of Qutayba bin Saeed, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, and Abu Salamah, both of them, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If the Imam believes, then they believe, for whoever whose belief coincides with the belief of the angels will be forgiven for what he has done.” He came forward from his sin.” On the authority of Suwayd bin Nasr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of them both."
"11359","On the authority of Ismail bin Masoud, on the authority of Yazid bin Zuray’, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If the imam says: ‘Not upon whom is anger nor gone astray,’ then say: ‘Ameen,’ for the angels say ‘Ameen.’” And the Imam says: Amen, so whoever’s assurance coincides with the assurance of the angels, his previous sins will be forgiven.”"
"11360","On the authority of Muhammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, And he said: “If one of you says: Amen, and the angels in heaven say: Amen, and one of them agrees with the other, he will be forgiven for his previous sins.” “His sin,” and on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Shuaib ibn al-Layth ibn Sa’d, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Ja’far ibn Rabi’ah, on the authority of Abd The Most Gracious, the Most Merciful, through Him (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11361","On the authority of Amr ibn Uthman, on the authority of Baqiyya, on the authority of Muhammad ibn al-Walid al-Zubaidi, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If the reader believes, then they believe, then the angels believe, so whoever’s belief is consistent with the belief of the angels, He will be forgiven for his previous sins.” On the authority of Saeed bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Sufyan bin Uyaynah, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, with it. On the authority of Amr bin Uthman, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Muslim, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, with it. Al-Nasa’i said: Al-Awza’i did not hear it from Al-Zuhri. On the authority of Al-Abbas bin Al-Walid bin Mazid, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Qurrah bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, with it. On the authority of Ahmad bin Harb, on the authority of Abu Muawiyah, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, with a chain of transmission. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11362","On the authority of Qutayba bin Saeed, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Sumayy, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If the imam says: God hears those who praise Him, then say: Our Lord, and to You is praise, for whoever’s speech agrees with the words of the angels, his sins will be forgiven.” “He came forward from his sin,” and on the authority of Suwayd bin Nasr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Malik, with it. On the authority of Muhammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, on the authority of Malik, with it. On the authority of Qutayba bin Saeed, on the authority of Yaqoub bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Salih, on the authority of his father, with (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11363","On the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ubaid, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, teaches us: “Do not hasten to bow before the imam, for when he says “Allahu Akbar,” then pronounce “Allahu Akbar,” and when he prostrates, then prostrate, and when he says: “Without anger.” upon them, nor those who go astray, so say: Amen. If the words of the angels agree with the words of the angels, those in the mosque will be forgiven. And if they say: God hears those who praise Him, then say “Our Lord, praise be to You.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11364","On the authority of Ahmad bin Sulaiman, on the authority of Ibn Nufail, on the authority of Muhammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Alaa bin Abdul Rahman bin Yaqoub, On the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Sa`id al-Khudri, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “When it was Friday, he would be at every door of “The doors of the mosque are angels who write down the first one after the first.” Hadith (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11365","On the authority of Yusuf bin Saeed bin Muslim, and Ibrahim bin Al-Hasan, both on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Ishaq, the client of Zaida, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The sun neither rises nor sets on a day Better than Friday, and there is no animal that does not fear Friday, except these two heavy things, the jinn and mankind, at every gate of The doors of the mosque are in two places, they are written as the first, so the first is like a man offering a camel, and like a man offering a cow, and like a man offering a sheep, and like a man offering A bird, or like a man offering an egg, so when the imam sits, the pages are folded.”"
"11366","On the authority of Qutayba bin Saeed, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Sumayy, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever takes a bath on Friday has done the ritual bath of impurity and goes, it is as if he sacrificed a camel, and whoever goes in the second hour, it is as if he sacrificed a cow, and whoever goes in at the third hour, it is as if he had sacrificed a ram, and whoever went at the fourth hour, it is as if he had sacrificed a hen, and whoever went at the fifth hour It is as if he had offered an egg, and when the imam came out, the angels were present, listening to the remembrance.” On the authority of Muhammad bin Salamah and Al-Harith bin Maskin, Both of them on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, on the authority of Malik, with (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11367","On the authority of Al-Rabi’ bin Sulaiman, on the authority of Shuaib bin Al-Layth, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Sumayyah, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “The angels sit on Friday at the gates of the mosque...”, the hadith, and on the authority of Qutaybah ibn Saeed, on the authority of Yaqoub bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Saleh, on the authority of his father, similarly (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11368","On the authority of Muhammad bin Mansour, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was informed of it: “ If it was Friday, there would be angels at every door of the mosque, that is, angels writing people down to their homes, first and foremost. So when the imam comes out, the pages are folded and they listen to the sermon. The one who migrates to prayer is like the Mahdi with a camel, then the one who follows him is like the Mahdi with a cow, then The next one is like the Mahdi, a ram, until he mentioned the hen and the egg.” On the authority of Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid, on the authority of Sufyan bin Uyaynah, With it (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11369","On the authority of Muhammad bin Khalid bin Khalili, on the authority of Bishr bin Shuaib bin Abi Hamza, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Al-Aghar, and Abu Salamah, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If it was Friday, it was at every door of the mosque.” Angels write down the first, then the first. When the imam sits, they fold the pages and sit and listen to the dhikr.” On the authority of Ahmad bin Amr bin Al-Sarh, Al-Harith bin Miskin, and Amr bin Sawad, three of them, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salman Al-Aghar, alone. On the authority of Suwayd bin Nasr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salman Al-Aghar, alone. On the authority of Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam, on the authority of Shuaib bin Al-Layth bin Saad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Khaled bin Yazid, on the authority of Saeed Bin Abi Hilal, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salman Al-Aghar, alone. On the authority of Sulayman bin Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Sulayman, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salman Al-Aghar, alone (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11370","On the authority of Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman bin Dawud, on the authority of Ishaq bin Bakr bin Mudar, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, On the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Hurmuz al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If it is Friday, On every door of the mosque there were angels writing down the first, then the first. When the imam sat, they folded the pages, and came and listened to the dhikr."
"11371","On the authority of Muhammad bin Bashar, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ja’far, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The sun does not rise or set on a day better or greater than the day of Friday, and there is no living creature.” Don't be afraid of Friday, except for these two burdens of jinn and mankind, and at every door there are two angels, writing the first and the first, like a man offering a camel. And like a man offering a cow, and like a man offering a sheep, and like a man offering a bird, and like a man offering an egg, then when the imam sits, the pages are folded.” And on the authority of Muhammad Bin Abdul-Ala, on the authority of Yazid bin Zurai, on the authority of Ruh bin Al-Qasim, on the authority of Al-Ala bin Abdul-Rahman, with it. On the authority of Qutayba bin Saeed, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz bin Abi Hazim, on the authority of Al-Alaa bin Abd al-Rahman, with it (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11372","On the authority of Ubaid bin Asbat bin Muhammad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, In his saying: “And the Fajr Qur’an. Indeed, the Fajr Qur’an is witnessed. He said: It is witnessed by the angels of the night and the angels of the day.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11373","On the authority of Amr bin Mansour, on the authority of Abdullah bin Raja’, on the authority of Hammam, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu al-Jawza al-Ruba’i, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When death approaches a believer, the angels of mercy attend him, and when his soul takes It is placed in a white silk garment, and it is taken to the gate of heaven. They say: We have not found a scent more pleasant than this. Then it is said: Let him rest. If he was in distress, he would be asked: What did so-and-so do? What did so-and-so do? And as for the infidel, when his soul is taken and he is taken to the gate of the earth? “The treasurers of the earth will say: We have never found an odor more foul-smelling than this, then it would reach the lower earth.”"
"11374","On the authority of Suleiman bin Dawud, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr bin Ata, on the authority of Saeed bin Yasar, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The dead are attended by the angels, so if he was a righteous man, he said: Come out.” O good soul, it was in a good body, come out virtuous, and bring good tidings with spirit and fragrance, and a Lord not angry, they even say that It comes out, then it is taken up to heaven, and it is opened for it, and it is said: Who is this? It is said: So-and-so, and it is said: Welcome good soul, it was? Into the good body, enter praiseworthy, and bring good tidings of spirit and fragrance, and a Lord not angry, and it will be said to it until it reaches the seventh heaven. And when it is a bad man, it is said, “Come out, O evil soul.” It is in an evil body. Come out, reprehensible, and give good tidings of good news. And twilight, and others of its form are pairs, so it is said that until it comes out, then it is taken up to the sky, and it is opened for it, and it is said: Who This? Then it is said: So-and-so, and it is said: No, the evil soul is welcome. It was in an evil body. Go out, blameworthy, and the gates of heaven will not be opened to you. \ (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"11375","On the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Sa`id, on the authority of Muadh ibn Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Qasamah ibn Zuhayr, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When a believer is present, the angels of mercy come to him with a white garment, and they say: Go out, satisfied and satisfactory.” From you to the Spirit of God and fragrance, and a Lord not angry, and it comes out like the sweetest scent of musk, to the point that some of them will give it to one another until They will bring it at the door, meaning the sky, and they will say: How pleasant is this wind that has come to you from the earth. Then they will bring with it the souls of the believers. They are more happy about him than any of you when someone comes to him in his absence, and they ask him: What did so-and-so do? What did so-and-so do? They say: Leave him, he was there The grief of the world, and when he says: Did he not come to you? They say: He will be taken to the nation of the abyss, and when the disbeliever comes, the angels of torment will come to him. With a wipe, and they will say: Come out, angry and condemned to the punishment of God. Then it will come out like the smell of a corpse, until they bring it to the gate of the earth. They will say: What is this smell that smells so bad that they bring the souls of disbelievers with it? On the authority of Ishaq bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Muadh bin Hisham, with (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11376","On the authority of Al-Abbas bin Muhammad, on the authority of Khalid bin Mukhlid, on the authority of Suleiman bin Bilal, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Abi Muzard, on the authority of Abu Al-Hubab Saeed bin Left, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is not a day when the servants wake up in the morning except that two angels descend.” One of them says: Oh God, give a successor to the spender, and the other says: Oh God, give the one who takes care of loss. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11377","On the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Muhammad bin Salam, on the authority of Hajjaj bin Muhammad, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Abi Talha , on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Amra, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “An angel calls out one of the gates of Heaven, saying: Who lends today and will be rewarded with it tomorrow? And another angel says: O God, give back to the spender, and give back to the one who takes possession of it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11378","On the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Ala’, on the authority of Abu Muawiyah, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “ “If a man invites his wife to his bed, and she refuses, and he spends the night angry with her, the angels curse her until the morning.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11379","On the authority of Muhammad bin Umar bin Hayaj, on the authority of Yahya bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Ibn Abjar, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Aghar Ibn Sulayk, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no people who remember God but the angels surround them.” And mercy enveloped them, and God mentioned them in His presence.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11380","On the authority of Abdul Wahhab bin Al-Hakam Al-Warraq, on the authority of Muadh bin Muadh, on the authority of Sufyan bin Saeed Al-Thawri, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Zazan, on the authority of Abdullah, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Indeed, God has angels who travel, conveying peace to me from my nation.” On the authority of Suwayd bin Nasr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Sufyan Al-Thawri, with it. On the authority of Muhammad bin Bashar, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Sufyan al-Thawri, with it. On the authority of Abu Bakr bin Ali, on the authority of Yusuf bin Marwan, on the authority of Fudayl, on the authority of Sufyan Al-Thawri, with it. On the authority of Al-Fadl bin Al-Abbas bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Mahbub bin Musa, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-A’mash, and Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Al-Sa'ib, with it (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11381","On the authority of Qutayba bin Saeed, on the authority of Yaqoub, on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Salih, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, And peace be upon him, he said: “If God loves a servant, he calls Gabriel and says: I loved so-and-so, so love him, and Gabriel loves him, then he calls Gabriel, the inhabitants of heaven: “Indeed, God loves so-and-so, so they love him, then He assigns for him acceptance on earth, and hatred like that.” And on the authority of Abdah Bin Abdullah, on the authority of Suwayd bin Amr Al-Kalbi, on the authority of Zuhair bin Muawiyah, on the authority of Al-Alaa bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Saleh, with it . On the authority of Qutayba bin Saeed, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Saleh, with it. On the authority of Al-Harith bin Miskin, on the authority of Ibn Al-Qasim, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Salih, with it"
"11382","On the authority of Al-Hussein bin Muhammad, and Muhammad bin Hisham, both on the authority of Bishr bin Al-Mufaddal, on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Saleh, on the authority of his father, on the authority of my father Huraira, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Angels do not accompany a company in which there is a dog or a bell.” On the authority of Harun bin Muhammad bin Bakkar bin Bilal, on the authority of Muhammad bin Issa bin Al-Qasim bin Sami’, on the authority of Ruh bin Al-Qasim, on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Saleh, with it (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11383","On the authority of Saeed bin Abdul Rahman Al Makhzoumi, on the authority of Sufyan bin Uyaynah, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The angels curse one of you if he points at his brother with an iron weapon, even if his brother belongs to his father and mother,” and on the authority of Shuaib bin Yusuf, on the authority of Yazid bin Harun, on the authority of Abdullah bin Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, with it. On the authority of Ahmad bin Salman al-Rahawi, on the authority of Yazid bin Harun, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, and Hisham bin Hassan, both on the authority of Ibn Sirin, with it . On the authority of Ahmad ibn Abdah, on the authority of Sulaym ibn Akhdar, on the authority of ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, similar to it, with a chain of transmission. On the authority of Qutayba, and Yahya bin Habib bin Arabi, both on the authority of Hammad bin Zaid, on the authority of Ayyub, and Yunus bin Ubaid, both on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, with a chain of narrators. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11384","On the authority of Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala, on the authority of al-Mu`tamir, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Nu`aym ibn Abi Hind, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: Abu Jahl said: Will Muhammad cover his face among the polytheists? It was said: Yes, so he said: By Al-Lat and Al-Uzza, if I saw him like that, I would have stepped on His neck, or I will rub his face in the dirt. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came while he was praying and allegedly stepped on his neck. He said: He did not suddenly surprise them while turning on his heels and protecting himself with his hand. It was said: What is the matter with you? ! He said: Between me and him is a ditch of fire, terror, and wings! Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If he had come close to me, the angels would have snatched him up, limb by limb.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"11385","On the authority of Muhammad bin Uthman bin Hakim, on the authority of Abu Nu’aym, on the authority of Muhammad bin Marwan al-Dahli, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “An angel descended from heaven and gave me good news that Fatima is the mistress of the women of my nation, and that Al-Hasan and Al-Hussein are the masters of the youth.” People of Paradise\ (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
